# Bans. Before boot, ban.txt gets three bans (tests/files/bans): badsite.example (all, permanent), highpower.example
# (newbies, level 61, above anyone, and not permanent, which only a file can make it) and *.old.example (permit,
# permanent). Every scenario connection's host is "scenario", and these bans are checked as nanny checks them:
# newbies when a new name is given, permit when an old one is. Smokegod (60) lists, refuses, lifts and adds bans;
# ban.txt is rewritten with the permanent ones, and removed when none are left. Then each kind of ban is tried on its
# own, and lifted: "scenario" for newbies keeps Freshling out (stock had no test for a ban with no *, so it let them
# in, #48); *nario for newbies keeps Greenhorn out; *cenari* for permit keeps Decimus out (stock tested the host
# inside the ban's name, the wrong way round, so let him in, #48); scenar* for permit keeps Quintus out; and
# *bigscenarios*, which "scenario" isn't inside, lets Seer through to the password prompt (stock kept him
# out). Then scenar* is banned twice,
# the second replacing the first, and lifted.
@place bans ban.txt
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
scroll 0
ban
ban somewhere weird
ban *
ban highpower.example
allow
allow nowhere
allow highpower.example
allow badsite.example
@file ban.txt
allow .old.example
@file ban.txt
ban scenario newbies
@connect new1
Freshling
@as god
allow scenario
ban *nario newbies
@connect new2
Greenhorn
@as god
allow nario
ban *cenari* permit
@connect dec
Decimus
@as god
allow cenari
permban scenar* permit
@file ban.txt
@connect quin
Quintus
@as god
allow scenar
ban *bigscenarios* permit
@connect seer
Seer
@as god
ban
allow bigscenarios
ban scenar*
ban scenar* newbies
ban
allow scenar
ban
@file ban.txt
